              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\begin{array}{r:c}4.3&2\\end{array}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "   2 is less than 5, so ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "4.32=4.30",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " to 1 decimal place",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The student replaced the digit after the cut with zero, giving two decimal places. Remove it instead; $4.32\\approx4.3$ to 1 decimal place.",
          "worked": "The critical digit is $2$. Since $2<5$, keep the tenths digit $3$ and remove the digits after the cut. Writing $4.30$ gives two decimal places; the requested answer has one.\n$$4.32\\approx4.3\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q6-c",
